// Copy this file to "Local.xcconfig" (gitignored, next to this one) and
// fill in your own Apple Development Team id. This keeps your personal
// team out of project.yml, which is shared/committed - and unlike an
// environment variable, Xcode reads this file directly at build time, so
// `xcodegen generate` never resets it.
//
// Find your team id in Xcode: select the LibrePaw target, Signing &
// Capabilities, pick your team, then look up DEVELOPMENT_TEAM under Build
// Settings (or in LibrePaw.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj).
//
// Not the parenthesized id `security find-identity -v -p codesigning`
// prints after "Apple Development: you@example.com": that's your
// certificate's own id, which for a free Personal Team differs from the
// team id, and Xcode then falls back to a team you have to fix by hand
// after every `xcodegen generate`.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOUR_TEAM_ID
